Z||000003||Oreif||08-28-2001||08:40 PM||||I have the Ocelot cross-drilled rotors on my car. The rotors are nice but the pads they give you with them are not. I switched to the "Performer" series pads from Autozone and they are far better. The only problem with the rotors is you'll hear a "swishing" noise after the brake pads have "seated" depending on the pads, some sound louder then others.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||08-28-2001||08:50 PM||||Drilled and slotted rotors are basically just for looks. In other words you’re just buying a fancy rotor that does the same thing as the stock ones do. In thew old days they used to vent a gas that would build up under hard braking but with today’s pad formulas that doesn’t happen anymore. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-28-2001||09:01 PM||||personally, i wouldnt use cross drilled ones for normal street driving. I use OEM ones. Ive seen too many crack at the holes from heat.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tina||08-28-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>I have the Ocelot cross-drilled rotors on my car.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Same here.<BR>Pretty much happy with  them.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B> The only problem with the rotors is you'll hear a "swishing" noise after the brake pads have "seated" depending on the pads, some sound louder then others.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yep, definitly noticeable.<BR>Seems to be coming from the front only though. <BR>But then again,<BR>Rear ones could just be masked by the engine noice.<BR>Scared the hell out of me though, the first time I heard that.<BR>Thought I blew a mayor leak in my vacum reservoir.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
